Subject: observe body drain before footer vertical space
Upstream-Status: Local embedding (not submitted)

term_end() enters the footer callback before print_man_foot() and
print_mdoc_foot() call term_vspace().  That call may flush still-buffered body
content before emitting the footer separator.  Emit a read-only boundary
immediately after term_newln() has drained the body, including when skipvsp
suppresses the following blank line.  An annotated sink can then retain the
body flush and filter only the real footer.  Formatter bytes are unchanged.

--- a/term.c
+++ b/term.c
@@ -677,6 +677,8 @@ term_vspace(struct termp *p)
 {
 
 	term_newln(p);
+	collect_emit(p, TERM_COLLECT_VSPACE_DRAIN, TERM_COLLECT_ENTER,
+	    TERM_COLLECT_FINAL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, TERMFONT_NONE);
 	if (0 < p->skipvsp)
 		p->skipvsp--;
 	else {
--- a/term.h
+++ b/term.h
@@ -70,7 +70,8 @@ enum term_collector_op {
 	TERM_COLLECT_FIELD_PLACE,
 	TERM_COLLECT_DIRECT,
 	TERM_COLLECT_DRAW,
-	TERM_COLLECT_ENDLINE
+	TERM_COLLECT_ENDLINE,
+	TERM_COLLECT_VSPACE_DRAIN
 };
 
 enum term_collector_phase {
